    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Jerusalem grew from a settlement by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gihon-spring">Gihon Spring</a> into a capital and sanctuary city, and was held in turn by Canaanites, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egyptians">Egyptians</a>, Judahites, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonians">Babylonians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a>, Muslim dynasties, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusaders</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, the British, Jordan and Israel.</li><li>It is holy to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaism">Judaism</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, and many of its buildings, from the Temple Mount to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-the-holy-sepulchre">Church of the Holy Sepulchre</a>, mark events that each faith tells in its own way.</li><li>Its history includes repeated sieges, destructions and expulsions, and the status of the city is still contested in the present.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>By one count, Jerusalem has been destroyed completely at least twice, besieged 23 times, captured and recaptured 44 times and attacked 52 times.</p></aside>
    </section>

